# Syntax highlighting on GitHub / Gitea (github-linguist)
#
# Linguist ships a fixed set of languages + grammars and cannot be taught Axle
# from inside a repo (that needs an upstream github-linguist PR), so a local
# VS Code grammar does NOT affect GitHub rendering. As a pragmatic remedy we map
# .axle to Rust — by far the closest supported grammar: fn / let / mut / pub /
# dyn / trait / struct / enum / use / match / self / as / is and //, ///, /** */
# comments all highlight correctly (only `class` / `constructor` are missed).
#
# `linguist-detectable=true` also counts .axle toward the repo language bar so
# the project reads as a code repo rather than "mostly Markdown/Python". Flip it
# to false if you would rather keep .axle out of the language statistics.
*.axle linguist-language=Rust linguist-detectable=true
